<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
  <title>Terms of Service — Contacts</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <main class="legal">
    <p class="legal-nav"><a href="/">Contacts</a> · <a href="/privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a> · <a href="#ru">По-русски</a></p>

    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="legal-date">Effective 17 October 2026</p>

    <p>Contacts (<a href="https://${domain}">${domain}</a>) is a private, non-commercial address book. By using it you agree to these terms. Contact: <a href="mailto:${email}">${email}</a>.</p>

    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <p>Accounts are created by the administrator for invited people only. Keep your password and app passwords to yourself; you are responsible for what is done with them. The administrator may suspend or delete an account that is misused.</p>

    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>The cards, photos and other data you add remain yours. You allow the service to store and process them only to show them to you, keep their history, and sync them with the devices and services you connect, such as CardDAV clients and Google Contacts. Add only data you are allowed to keep, and respect the privacy of the people in your address book.</p>

    <h2>Google Contacts</h2>
    <p>Connecting Google Contacts lets the service read and change your Google contacts and contact groups to keep them in sync with this address book, which is treated as the source of truth. You can disconnect at any time in the settings. Your use of Google is also governed by Google's own terms. How Google data is handled is described in the <a href="/privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Do not use the service to break the law, to send spam, or to try to access other users' data or disrupt the service.</p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>The service is provided free of charge, "as is", without any warranty. It may change, be interrupted or be shut down. Keep your own copy of important data: the app can export your address book as a vCard file at any time. To the extent permitted by law, the operator is not liable for loss of data or any damages arising from use of the service.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>These terms may change; the current version is always on this page.</p>

    <hr>

    <section id="ru" lang="ru">
      <h1>Условия использования</h1>
      <p class="legal-date">Действуют с 17 октября 2026 г.</p>
      <p>«Контакты» — частная некоммерческая адресная книга. Учётные записи создаёт администратор только для приглашённых. Пароли и пароли приложений храните в тайне. Ваши данные остаются вашими: сервис хранит и обрабатывает их только чтобы показывать вам, вести историю и синхронизировать с подключёнными вами устройствами и сервисами, в том числе Google Контактами (книга — источник истины; отключить можно в любой момент в настройках). Не используйте сервис для нарушения закона, спама и доступа к чужим данным. Сервис бесплатный и предоставляется «как есть», без гарантий; он может меняться или прекратить работу — держите свою копию, книгу можно в любой момент выгрузить в vCard. Вопросы: <a href="mailto:${email}">${email}</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
